 cat_missing_file\n   237→    description: 'Non-existent file prints error to stderr, exits 1, continues processing. Setup: real.txt contains \"data\\n\", nonexistent.txt does not exist'\n   238→    inputs:\n   239→      args: [\"nonexistent.txt\", \"real.txt\"]\n   240→      stdin: null\n   241→      env: []\n   242→    normalization: none\n   243→    expected:\n   244→      exit_code: 1\n   245→      stdout: \"data\\n\"\n   246→      stderr_contains: \"nonexistent.txt\"\n   247→    traces:\n   248→      - prd006-cat R5.2\n   249→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a37955b4-bb6b-4f86-bd5e-f3601e429336","uuid":"568deed4-a8c3-4259-a4d6-c860a2034744","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/297/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.1.yaml","content":"id: test-rel01.1\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel01.1 — cat specification and differential test\"\nrelease: rel01.1\n\ntraces:\n  - rel01.1-uc001-cat\n  - prd006-cat R1\n  - prd006-cat R2\n  - prd006-cat R3\n  - prd006-cat R4\n  - prd006-cat R5\n\npreconditions:\n  - ./bin/cat exists (built via mage build).\n  - Reference binary gcat is installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/cat/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n  - \"cat: no normalization is applied; cat output is deterministic. Binary test inputs are specified as hex escape sequences.\"\n\ntest_cases:\n  - name: cat_default_passthrough\n    description: 'No flags, text file content passes through verbatim. Setup: file1.txt contains \"hello\\nworld\\n\"'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"file1.txt\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R1.1\n      - prd006-cat R1.5\n\n  - name: cat_binary_passthrough\n    description: No flags, binary input (all byte values 0x00-0xFF) passes through without corruption.\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: \"\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\x02...\\\\xfe\\\\xff (all 256 byte values)\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: identical 256 bytes as input\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R1.4\n\n  - name: cat_line_numbering_n\n    description: -n flag prepends line numbers to all lines including blank lines.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-n\"]\n      stdin: \"alpha\\n\\nbeta\\n\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"     1\\talpha\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tbeta\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R2.1\n\n  - name: cat_line_numbering_b\n    description: -b flag prepends line numbers only to non-blank lines.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-b\"]\n      stdin: \"first\\n\\n\\nsecond\\n\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"     1\\tfirst\\n\\n\\n     2\\tsecond\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R2.2\n      - prd006-cat R2.4\n\n  - name: cat_squeeze_blanks\n    description: -s collapses consecutive blank lines to one.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-s\"]\n      stdin: \"a\\n\\n\\n\\nb\\n\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"a\\n\\nb\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R3.1\n\n  - name: cat_show_nonprinting\n    description: -v displays non-printing characters with caret and M- notation.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-v\"]\n      stdin: \"\\\\x01\\\\x09\\\\x1b\\\\x7f\\\\x80\\\\xff\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"^A\\\\x09^[^?M-^@M-^?\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R4.1\n      - prd006-cat R4.2\n\n  - name: cat_show_ends\n    description: -E appends \"$\" before each newline.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-E\"]\n      stdin: \"line one\\nline two\\n\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"line one$\\nline two$\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R4.3\n\n  - name: cat_show_tabs\n    description: -T displays tabs as \"^I\".\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-T\"]\n      stdin: \"col1\\\\tcol2\\\\tcol3\\n\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"col1^Icol2^Icol3\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R4.4\n\n  - name: cat_show_all\n    description: -A is equivalent to -vET combined.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-A\"]\n      stdin: \"\\\\x01\\\\thello\\n\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"^A^Ihello$\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R4.5\n\n  - name: cat_flag_e\n    description: -e is equivalent to -vE (show non-printing and show ends).\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-e\"]\n      stdin: \"\\\\x01hello\\n\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"^Ahello$\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R4.6\n\n  - name: cat_flag_t\n    description: -t is equivalent to -vT (show non-printing and show tabs).\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-t\"]\n      stdin: \"\\\\x01\\\\thello\\n\"\n      env: []\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"^A^Ihello\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd006-cat R4.7\n\n  - name: cat_flag_u_accepted\n    description: -u flag is accepted without error, output unchan